  "notes": [
    "Complete list: 14 actions and 3 advanced feedbacks, all registered in single calls in pds.js (init_actions line 373, init_feedbacks line 267). Source is a single ES-module file.",
    "Protocol: line-based text over TCP port 3000 (hard-coded, pds.js:66) to the config host. Every action shares one callback that builds `<ACTION-ID> -<optionId> <value>` for each non-empty option and sends it with a trailing CR (pds.js:424-444): the action ids are the PDS command names and the option ids are the command's flag letters. An empty text option (e.g. ISEL filenumber) is omitted.",
    "Dropdown ids keep their source type: input/logo/mode ids are NUMBERS, while the option defaults are STRINGS ('1', '0', '4'). The type mismatch is in the source.",
    "Input lists (ISEL, PIPISEL, and the preview/program feedbacks) depend on the config 'variant' (PDS-701 = 1, PDS-901 = 2, PDS-902 = 3, from the config dropdown whose ids are numbers and default is the string '1'): see choicesNote. optionsComplete stays true; only the offered input ids vary.",
    "The config dropdown uses self.PDS_VARIANT, which is first assigned in init_actions (pds.js:376), while getConfigFields reads it; it can be undefined when the config UI is built before init has run. Not catalogued further.",
    "The feedback checks `states[...] === parseInt(options.input)` against states polled every 4 s (PREVIEW/PROGRAM/LOGOSEL queries) and updated from TAKE/ISEL responses (pds.js:37-44, 99-132). Feedback colour defaults: fg white 16777215 for all, bg green 65280 (preview) or red 16711680 (program, logo).",
    "The action callback tests `!this._isConnected` (the method, never called), which is always false, so the connection guard never triggers; if the socket is missing, send throws.",
    "Textinput regex values (ISEL file number 1-64; TRNTIME seconds 0-12 with an optional single decimal) are given as they evaluate at runtime.",
    "Built on @companion-module/base ~1.11.0: options do not support expressions. Presets and variables are not catalogued (none are defined in pds.js)."
  ]
}
